# repetitions:
# CSES 1069, Repetitions (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1069), in our own words: a
# string over the four letters A, C, G and T; the length of its longest run, a stretch
# of consecutive positions that hold one letter. The input is a Scott list
# (corpora/library/prelude/list) of the letters, each a binary natural
# (corpora/library/binary/natural), A = 0, C = 1, G = 2 and T = 3, and the answer a
# binary natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: every contiguous segment of the list is
# built (the segments are, for each place the list is cut at, the nonempty prefixes of
# what follows), those whose letters are all equal are kept, and the greatest length
# among them is taken. Its reading builds and checks about n squared segments of up to
# n letters; the replacement the family asks for is one linear scan that counts the
# run ending at each letter, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since each consumes
# the finite list of letters, of segments or of one segment; the branches that a Scott
# boolean discards are never read. The program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and
# P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of
# Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ _ binary_maximum _
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items nil λ head tail. cons (cons head nil) λ. map (cons head) λ. self tail
  )
λ prefixes
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items nil λ _ tail. append (prefixes items) λ. self tail
  )
λ segments
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items true λ head tail. tail true λ next _. merge_binary_equality head next (self tail) false
  )
λ equal_letters
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λ self count items. items count λ _ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self most segment_list
    . segment_list most
      λ segment rest
      . self (equal_letters segment (binary_maximum most (count_from binary_zero segment)) most) rest
  )
λ longest
. (λtuple. tuple λletters. longest binary_zero (segments letters))
λ repetitions
. export repetitions
